;As of revision 6.00 of AOS/VS the system call numbers that are used
;when entering the Agent will be different than those system call
;numbers used when calling the Kernel.
 
;When defining a new system call which relies on the kernel for
;processing, an additional symbol must be defined to represent the
;system call number as the kernel sees it. The kernel calls begin at
;4000(8) and continue sequentially. This means that there is no longer
;a one-to-one correspondence between kernel and agent system call
;numbers. The kernel system call symbols differ from agent system call
;symbols in the fact that the "." is replaced by a "0". Please see the
;definition of the ?SONS system call for an example.

;The new numbering scheme for kernel calls start at 4300. The existing
;system calls from 0-277 have been redefined using the new scheme for
;consistency with new symbols. These symbols should only be used when
;making LCALLs to the kernel. (For Agent and PMGR that is usually
;through the SYCA and SYCA1 mechanisms.)

.DUSR   ?0CREATE=4000           ;CREATE FILE
.DUSR   ?0CREA  =4000           ;CREATE FILE
.DUSR   ?0DELETE=4001           ;DELETE FILE
.DUSR   ?0DELE  =4001           ;DELETE FILE
.DUSR   ?0RENAME=4002           ;RENAME A FILE
.DUSR   ?0RENA  =4002           ;RENAME A FILE
.DUSR   ?0MEM   =4003           ;RETURN MEMORY LIMITS
.DUSR   ?0GCHN  =4004           ;CHANGE THE CURRENT PROGRAM
.DUSR   ?0PSTAT =4005           ;PROCESS STATUS
.DUSR   ?0PSTA  =4005           ;PROCESS STATUS
.DUSR   ?0DPMGR =4006           ;DEFINE PERIPHERAL MANAGER
.DUSR   ?0DPMG  =4006           ;DEFINE PERIPHERAL MANAGER
.DUSR   ?0RDB   =4007           ;READ A PHYSICAL BLOCK
.DUSR   ?0WRB   =4011           ;WRITE A PHYSICAL BLOCK
.DUSR   ?0GPROC =4013           ;CREATE A PROCESS
.DUSR   ?0GPRO  =4013           ;CREATE A PROCESS
.DUSR   ?0MEMI  =4014           ;ALLOCATE MEMORY
.DUSR   ?0DELA  =4015           ;SUSPEND FOR A TIME PERIOD
                                ; (16 BIT CALL ONLY)
.DUSR   ?0INTWT =4016           ;WAIT FOR A CONSOLE INTERRUPT
.DUSR   ?0INTW  =4016           ;WAIT FOR A CONSOLE INTERRUPT
.DUSR   ?0MBTU  =4021           ;MOVE BYTES TO PROCESS
.DUSR   ?0MBFU  =4023           ;MOVE BYTES FROM PROCESS
